  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.4.2: language-quality pass ported back from the Synthelion (Python port) 1.2.0 quality review. Fixed: negation particles (\"non\"/\"not\"/\"ne...pas\"/\"no\"/\"nicht\"/\"não\"/\"不\") were being stripped as ordinary function words at every compression level, silently inverting sentence meaning -- now protected in eng/ita/fra/spa/deu/por/zho, with prefix-aware matching for Chinese compounds (\"不是\"/\"不管\"). Fixed Italian \"subito\" (adverb, \"immediately\") being mis-lemmatised to \"subire\" (verb, \"to undergo\") via a UD homograph-contaminated lemma entry -- LemmaOrLower now skips a lemma substitution when the surface form is POS-tagged ADV and the lemma differs. Added CavemanCjkSegmenter: dictionary-based Chinese word segmentation (DAG + dynamic-programming longest-match path, jieba's non-ML dictionary algorithm re-implemented rather than taken as a dependency) -- Chinese previously had no word segmentation at all, so compression and language detection both silently no-op'd beyond punctuation stripping. Repaired real mojibake corruption (UTF-8 mis-decoded as Windows-1252 at an earlier pipeline stage) in worddata/zho.yaml(.br), zho.pos.yaml.br, and _index.br (10 further affected languages: ben, ell, eng, heb, hin, jpn, kor, mar, tha, vie). Fixed language-detection data contamination: \"john\" (an English name) removed from 16 languages' function-word lists, \"ha\"/\"e\" (Italian words, not French) removed from French's list, and \"ate\" removed from Portuguese's exclusive markers (collided with English's own \"ate\"). All changes are additive and backward-compatible; 14 new regression tests (311/311 total).",
